# InnBucks cell — ZIMBABWE (Fineract core). NON-SECRET policy only.
#
#     set -a; source deploy/cells/cell.zw.env; set +a
#     set -a; source deploy/fineract/.env;     set +a     # secrets, gitignored
#     ./deploy/fineract/provision-cell.sh
#
# See cell.example.env for what each key means and why.

CELL_CURRENCY=USD
PRODUCT_NAME="InnBucks Wallet"
PRODUCT_SHORT=IBWL

# Script defaults are already ZW-shaped, so both code lists are left unset.

# ─── Bank operational roles ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Derived from the 2026-09 internal UAT run. The names below are VERBATIM from
# this cell's own GET /v1/roles (read 2026-09-18) — note the uppercase "TEST"
# prefix and that Internal Audit is not "Auditor". An earlier revision of this
# file guessed them from the UAT script; the names did not match, and because
# step 6b used to CREATE a missing role, the run made three empty roles nobody
# held and reported success. 6b now refuses to create and names the closest
# existing role instead. If the bank renames a role, change it HERE.
#
# Who holds each, for review (same read):
#   TEST Operations Manager (27)                             Juliet
#   TEST Operations Manager Checker (19)                     Daniel
#   TEST Internal Audit (26)                                 Michael
#   TEST Risk Manager (22)                                   Marcos
#   TEST Branch Operations Supervisor / Branch Manager (18)  Gibson, Kim
#   TEST Compliance Manager (23)                             Emma
#   TEST Financial Controller (21)                           Olivia
#   TEST Head of Credit (25)                                 Robert
#   TEST Product Administrator (24)                          Charlotte
#
# Why each grant exists:
#   Operations Manager   UNDOTRANSACTION_SAVINGSACCOUNT — UAT rows 17/18/129/130:
#                        "no option to reverse a transaction". This is the maker
#                        side of a teller-posting reversal.
#                        RECOVERYPAYMENT_LOAN — UAT row 105: no way to post a
#                        recovery against a written-off loan. Needs the
#                        product's incomeFromRecoveryAccountId mapped too.
#   Ops Mgr Checker      UNDOTRANSACTION_SAVINGSACCOUNT_CHECKER — the approver
#                        for the reversal above. Without it the reversal parks
#                        into an inbox nobody can act on.
#   Internal Audit       READ_AUDIT — UAT row 155, but see the caveat below:
#                        READ_AUDIT buys GET /v1/audits, NOT the maker-checker
#                        inbox, and the inbox is not a permission problem.
#   Risk Manager         the unblock + hold side of the block family. BLOCKDEBIT
#                        already worked in UAT (row 42); these complete it.
#                        CREATE_USER_CHECKER — UAT row 171.
#
# THE CHECKER GRANTS. MAKER_CHECKER_TASKS below flags EIGHT tasks; every one of
# them needs a role holding the matching '<CODE>_CHECKER', or the command parks
# into an inbox nobody can act on — which is the UAT's original complaint with a
# different cause. An earlier revision of this file flagged all eight and
# granted exactly one checker permission. The other seven are below, each
# assigned to the role the UAT scenario names:
#
#   row 45        UPDATE_CLIENTIDENTIFIER_CHECKER  "Compliance clears a client-
#                                                   identifier change"
#   rows 107,111  CREATE_JOURNALENTRY_CHECKER      "Controller clears journal /
#                                                   branch reversal"
#   row 90        WRITEOFF_LOAN_CHECKER            "Finance clears write-off"
#   row 93        APPROVE_LOAN_CHECKER             "HoC clears CM approval"
#   row 94        UPDATE_LOANPRODUCT_CHECKER       "HoC clears product pricing"
#   row 143       CREATE_LOANPRODUCT_CHECKER       "Checker clears new loan
#                                                   product" — the ONE row that
#                                                   does not name a role. Put on
#                                                   Product Administrator, who
#                                                   owns the product catalogue;
#                                                   move it to Head of Credit if
#                                                   the bank says otherwise.
#   row 171       CREATE_USER_CHECKER              "Risk clears user creation"
#
# All eight checker codes are confirmed seeded (checked against the changelogs
# 2026-09-18). Note these are INVISIBLE to GET /v1/permissions, which filters
# '%_CHECKER' out — use GET /v1/roles/{id}/permissions to verify them.
BANK_ROLE_GRANTS="TEST Operations Manager=UNDOTRANSACTION_SAVINGSACCOUNT,RECOVERYPAYMENT_LOAN;TEST Operations Manager Checker=UNDOTRANSACTION_SAVINGSACCOUNT_CHECKER;TEST Internal Audit=READ_AUDIT;TEST Risk Manager=UNBLOCKDEBIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT,BLOCKCREDIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT,UNBLOCKCREDIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT,HOLDAMOUNT_SAVINGSACCOUNT,RELEASEAMOUNT_SAVINGSACCOUNT,CREATE_USER_CHECKER;TEST Compliance Manager=UPDATE_CLIENTIDENTIFIER_CHECKER;TEST Financial Controller=CREATE_JOURNALENTRY_CHECKER,WRITEOFF_LOAN_CHECKER;TEST Head of Credit=APPROVE_LOAN_CHECKER,UPDATE_LOANPRODUCT_CHECKER;TEST Product Administrator=CREATE_LOANPRODUCT_CHECKER"

# CAVEAT on the audit grant, verified in the fork 2026-09-18. READ_AUDIT gates
# GET /v1/audits (AuditsApiResource:76). The maker-checker inbox
# (GET /v1/makercheckers) has NO permission check at all — any authenticated
# user may call it — but it returns only entries whose '<ACTION>_<ENTITY>_CHECKER'
# permission the caller holds. So "let the auditor see the maker-checker log" is
# not a READ_* grant: it needs ALL_FUNCTIONS or CHECKER_SUPER_USER, and
# CHECKER_SUPER_USER ALSO confers the power to approve one's own parked commands
# (PortfolioCommandSourceWritePlatformServiceImpl:129 bypasses the same-maker
# check for it). That is the opposite of what an audit role should hold, so it is
# deliberately NOT granted — raise it with the bank as a design question.
#
# Second caveat: GET /v1/audits is office-scoped by an INNER join
# (AuditReadPlatformServiceImpl:121-124). Only a HEAD-OFFICE user (hierarchy '.')
# sees everything; a branch-attached auditor loses every row with a NULL
# office_id — product, config and role changes, i.e. exactly what an internal
# auditor is looking for. Check which office the auditor is attached to before
# concluding the grant did not work.

# ─── Maker-checker ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dual-control set the UAT script exercised. Deliberately NOT included:
# anything the middleware issues (the script refuses those anyway), and the
# five actions with no seeded _CHECKER row.
MAKER_CHECKER_TASKS="CREATE_JOURNALENTRY,UNDOTRANSACTION_SAVINGSACCOUNT,WRITEOFF_LOAN,APPROVE_LOAN,CREATE_LOANPRODUCT,UPDATE_LOANPRODUCT,CREATE_USER,UPDATE_CLIENTIDENTIFIER"

# Still 0: the CBS console does not yet treat a 200 carrying
# "rollbackTransaction": true as "submitted for approval" rather than "done".
# Flip to 1 in the same change that ships that handling, not before.
ENABLE_MAKER_CHECKER=0

# ─── GL control accounts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UNSET until the ZW chart's control-account glCodes are confirmed. Fill from:
#   api GET /v1/glaccounts | jq -r '.[]|select(.manualEntriesAllowed==true)|"\(.glCode)\t\(.name)"'
# and pick the portfolio / control / receivable / suspense accounts.
CONTROL_ACCOUNT_GLCODES=""

ASSERT_LOAN_PRODUCT_ACCOUNTING=1
